recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":1.8544999999999998,"recipe":false,"temperature":95.0}],"name":"Sponge","notes":["This is pre-ferment. It\u0027s mixed with other doughs to help flavor and speed up development.","Speed up fermentation and yeast development by using warm water.    \nI do about 20 seconds in the microwave. Add flour/sugar mix then yeast."]},{"archived":false,"category":1,"id":18,"ingredients":[{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":0.48,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":100,"percent":0.035,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":1,"percent":0.96,"recipe":true}],"name":"Rustic Boule","notes":["650g total flour for one good sized loaf.   \nCombine poolish and allow to ferment overnight.   \nA whole wheat poolish will help improve whole wheat doughs.","Add all additional ingredients and mix/knead until fully combined.   \nStretch and fold the dough at 45 minute intervals.   \nWhen the dough retains its shape (usually after two or three intervals) form into boules and proof until doubled in size.","Bake 450F for about 20 minutes. Covered in cast iron dutch oven."]},{"archived":false,"category":14,"id":17,"ingredients":[{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":86,"percent":0.2,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":141,"percent":0.6,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":99,"percent":0.016,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":150,"percent":0.015,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":12,"percent":0.172,"recipe":false}],"name":"Cinnamon Roll Dough","notes":["450g total flour fills a half bakers sheet.   \nThis is a good dough for donuts, sticky breads. It\u0027s sweet and fluffy.   \nMelt the butter with the milk in the microwave. Let cool enough so you don\u0027t kill the yeast.","Mix dry ingredients in mixer bowl and add wet with dough hook running.   \nLet ferment/develop 3 hours.","Spread out and roll then cut and let rise/proof 1 hour.   \nBake at 350F for ~35min.","Substitutes  \nMilk/Buttermilk/Almond Milk   \nButter/Margarine/Shortening  \nSugar/Splenda/other sweetener.  \nWorks pretty well with most combinations, but I like using Almond milk.   \nI think they might come out fluffier."]},{"archived":false,"category":14,"id":16,"ingredients":[{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":134,"percent":0.2,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":0.233,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":187,"percent":0.14,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":181,"percent":0.016,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":3,"percent":0.54,"recipe":true},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":86,"percent":0.22,"recipe":false}],"name":"Sweet Bread","notes":["I usually use a bundt pan for this bread.   \n500g total flour fills a standard bundt pan.","This bread works best without too much handling.   \nUse paddle to do a quick mix of ingredients.   \nI like to coat the dough with a spray of canola oil.","First rise 3 hours.       \nProof about 1½ hours in pan.   \n\nSpray your pan or the bread will stick.","350F for 45-50 minutes tented with foil helps prevent burning."]},{"archived":false,"category":1,"id":15,"ingredients":[{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":134,"percent":0.087,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":86,"percent":0.079,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":99,"percent":0.02,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":125,"percent":0.632,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":150,"percent":0.012,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":187,"percent":0.105,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false}],"name":"White Bread","notes":["350g total flour makes 4 buns.   \nThis is a great dough for hamburger and hotdog buns or a loaf for sandwiches.","Mix all liquid ingredients then add to dry ingredients   \nKnead using  dough hook for 8 minutes.   \nDough should be a little bit tacky.","Cover and let rise 1½ - 2 hours until double size.   \nShape into tight bouls about 3 oz for buns.","Preheat to 400F for rolls and buns (small) and bake for 15 minutes.   \nOr 30 minutes at 350F for a loaf.   \nLet cool. These are good the next day too. Super soft and chewy."]},{"archived":false,"category":1,"id":10,"ingredients":[{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":150,"percent":0.0055000000000000005,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":99,"percent":0.0195,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":15,"percent":0.050199999999999995,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":0.5996,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":87,"percent":0.037000000000000005,"recipe":false}],"name":"Pretzels","notes":["About 420g total flour is good for a ½ bakers sheet.   \nThese are great rolled into a snake shape and cut into pretzel tots.","Mix dry ingredients in mixer with dough hook. Add oil to dry ingredients then add the water.   \nKnead dough a few minutes on medium mixer with dough hook. Should be a little sticky.","Refrigerate overnight or couple of days.","Pull from fridge and shape. Dip in solution of 60 grams baking soda to 2 cups boiling water.   \nSprinkle with rock salt.   \nBake at 400F for 15 minutes.   \nLet cool a few minutes and enjoy. These are tasty!"]},{"archived":false,"category":1,"id":8,"ingredients":[{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":156,"percent":0.25,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":99,"percent":0.018000000000000002,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":150,"percent":0.02,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":0.75,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":0.8,"recipe":false}],"name":"Focaccia","notes":["500g total flour fills out ½ bakers sheet  ( good for a thick crust pizza as well )   \n560g total flour for focaccia on ½ bakers sheet which is about 2 cups water and a splash of oil is good.","Let ferment a few hours. Kneading is best but a few folds works too.   \nAnd then proof for 1½ hours.  \nBake at 450F 12-15 minutes.","I like to preheat the bakers sheet and place the silicone mat with the proofed dough.   \nI think it helps the bottom of the crust get toasty."]},{"archived":false,"category":1,"id":6,"ingredients":[{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":150,"percent":0.011000000000000001,"recipe":false},{"flour":true,"hydration":false,"id":154,"percent":1.0,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":false,"id":181,"percent":0.018600000000000002,"recipe":false},{"flour":false,"hydration":true,"id":109,"percent":0.74725,"recipe":false}],"name":"Basic Bread","notes":["An easy bread that\u0027s quick to prepare.   \nMix all the ingredients and let ferment overnight to develop flavor.  \nGive it a couple of folds and then shape it. Proof 1-1½ hours.   \nBake at 450F for 30-35 minutes covered and an additional 10-15 minutes uncovered for crust.   \nWorks well in cast iron dutch oven."]}],"version":2}